


VSWAPON(2V)         UNIX Programmer's Manual          VSWAPON(2V)



NAME
     vswapon - add a swap device for interleaved paging/swapping

SYNOPSIS
     vswapon(name)
     char *name;

DESCRIPTION
     _V_s_w_a_p_o_n makes the argument block device available to the
     system for allocation for paging and swapping.  The number
     of blocks to be made available, as well as the names of all
     potentially available devices are known to the system, and
     are present in the system configuration file (e.g.
     /usr/src/sys/conf/confhp.c).

SEE ALSO
     swapon(8)

BUGS
     There is no way to stop swapping on a disk so that the pack
     may be dismounted.

     This call is peculiar to this version of UNIX.
































